%N A400548 E.g.f. A(x) satisfies A(x) = 1/(1 - x*A(x)^x).
%H A400548 Seiichi Manyama, <a href="/A400548/b400548.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 0..394</a>
%F A400548 a(0) = 1; a(n) = n! * Sum_{j=0..floor((n-1)/2)} (n-j)^j * Sum_{k=j+1..n-j} binomial(n-j-1,k-1) * Stirling1(k-1,j)/k!.
%F A400548 a(n) ~ n^(n-1) * sqrt(1 - 2*r*log(r)/(1+r)) / (sqrt(2*r^((r-1)/(r+1)) - r - 1) * exp(n) * r^(n + 1/2 + 2/(1+r))), where r = 0.4214518303433019663622598075106479936652984008256318444468... is the root of the equation (1 - r^(1 - 2*r/(1+r))) = r^(2/(1+r)). - _Vaclav Kotesovec_, Sep 30 2026
